    "claim": "The pad tools need a tool-calling arm (VLLM, OPENAI, ANTHROPIC, GEMINI, OLLAMA). The CLAUDECODE arm never returns kind:tool_calls - Claude Code runs its own loop and ignores the page's tools - so a chat on that arm cannot stage, eval, or snapshot. Letting an out-of-page agent (CLAUDECODE delegate, MCP client, server-side tool_loop) drive the pad needs a server->page bridge: flowlang's fire_event + the page's subscribe_event websocket push is the substrate (the abandoned long-poll eval_pump never worked: the Rust command looked up a JS function as a backend command). Note `newbound mcp` is a separate process from the web server, so an MCP-side bridge must forward to the running server.",
