    "claim": "Snapshot pixels reach the model through agentloop's chatTurn: execTool may resolve {content, images:[paths]}; the round's images ride ONE user message ([SNAPSHOT IMAGES ...]) after all of that round's tool results, because tool messages carry no images on every wire (OpenAI's cannot) - the user-message images path is the one every chat_llm dialect already renders. agent.chat strips the images from earlier [SNAPSHOT IMAGES messages at the start of each new turn so requests don't grow without bound. capture() rasterizes via cloned subtree + inlined computed styles (inherited props compared with the parent, the rest with the tag's default from a sandbox iframe) -> SVG foreignObject -> canvas; pseudo-elements, scroll positions, iframes, shadow DOM and web fonts are lost.",
